    <briefdescription>
<para>A <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell" kindref="compound">Cell</ref> that defines its own material points, like a finite element defines its quadrature points. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>In contrast to a plain <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell" kindref="compound">Cell</ref>, which integrates over whatever material points currently lie inside it, a cell element requests a fixed set of material points: the host framework queries <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell_element_1a808f7adb2b75965e2b3850959ca6b24b" kindref="member">getNMaterialPoints()</ref>, <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell_element_1aa76998dd6353741c07d22194001fa3e1" kindref="member">getRequestedMaterialPointCoordinates()</ref> and <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell_element_1a8a72361058b270c80dc43b3998ab7778" kindref="member">getRequestedMaterialPointVolumes()</ref>, creates one material point per request (e.g. at the points of the quadrature rule passed to <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_registry_1_1_cell_element_factory" kindref="compound">Marmot::Registry::CellElementFactory</ref>), and assigns them back with <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_cell_1a8b58710a1cd58fad5b96e5ab88be5d63" kindref="member">Cell::assignMaterialPoints()</ref>. The cell element may additionally carry its own state variables.</para>
<para>Instances are created by name via <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_registry_1_1_cell_element_factory" kindref="compound">Marmot::Registry::CellElementFactory</ref>. No concrete cell element is contained in Marmot at present. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
